From 68d4d8fbb6001e3e5252b18729a670f1c1ac8367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Lukschander <oliver.lukschander@golf.at>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:26:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: dcp: prefer non-fixed-output pipelines for a DP
 tunnel route

apple_dcp_tb_dp_tunnel()'s route scoring used plain
dcp_typec_route_score() (CRTC index only), unlike the pre-port
dcp_typec_route_score_usb4() it replaced, which penalized a pipeline
with its own fixed output (dcpext0, HDMI-capable) so a tunnel would
prefer the Type-C-only pipeline (dcpext1) instead. The reference PR
(t8103) has no equivalent bias because t8103 has a single dcpext.

Confirmed on real hardware (candidate 0127's first boot): the tunnel
routed to dcp@289c00000 (dcpext0) instead of dcp@315c00000 (dcpext1,
every prior candidate's own working AFK target) -- dcpext0 has a fixed
phy@1303000000 dependency (HDMI analog), dcpext1 does not. DCP actually
completed a genuine AUX/DPRX handshake for the first time this whole
project (DPRX_DONE=1, "ACIO AUX completed") -- validating the
underlying architecture -- but retried the connection once and gave up
both times (release_display), consistent with dcpext0 having the wrong
plane/CRTC/scanout wiring for a Type-C-tunneled source even though the
physical AUX signal itself succeeded.

Restores the same fixed_phy penalty dcp_typec_route_score_usb4() used
to apply, inline in apple_dcp_tb_dp_tunnel()'s own scoring loop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 01d08a1..6c24ef6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -595,6 +595,23 @@ int apple_dcp_tb_dp_tunnel(struct device_node *connector_np, unsigned int dpin,
 		if (!dcp_typec_route_available(candidate))
 			continue;
 		score = dcp_typec_route_score(candidate);
+		/*
+		 * j416s-specific, not in the reference (t8103 has a single
+		 * dcpext): prefer a pipeline with no fixed output of its own
+		 * (dcpext1, USB-C only) over one that can also drive a fixed
+		 * HDMI/DP output (dcpext0). dcp_typec_route_available()
+		 * already excludes dcpext0 while its fixed output is
+		 * actually live, but a plain CRTC-index comparison otherwise
+		 * lets dcpext0 win a tunnel route whenever nothing is
+		 * plugged into HDMI -- confirmed on real hardware (2026-09-24
+		 * candidate 0127's first boot: the tunnel routed to
+		 * dcp@289c00000/dcpext0 instead of dcp@315c00000/dcpext1,
+		 * every prior candidate's own working AFK target). Matches
+		 * the same bias the pre-port dcp_typec_route_score_usb4()
+		 * applied for exactly this reason.
+		 */
+		if (candidate->dcp->fixed_phy)
+			score += 100;
 		if (score < best_score) {
 			best = candidate;
 			best_score = score;
-- 
2.55.0

